WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.520
Two little words: «avant que»,

2
00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:06.340
before, and «après que», after.

3
00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:07.800
Now watch the verb.

4
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.380
Before he leaves: «avant qu'il parte».

5
00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:12.920
After he left: «après qu'il est parti».

6
00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:15.080
Same verb, same person.

7
00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:18.380
But only one of them puts
the verb in a special form.

8
00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:20.840
So why does before need a special verb,

9
00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:22.830
when after doesn't?

10
00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.510
In this mission, you'll open five doors,

11
00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:28.240
each hiding a group of these little words.

12
00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:30.430
Then you'll build sentences in the lab,

13
00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:34.250
choosing between «avant
de» and «avant que».

14
00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:37.570
Your mission: work out why
one little word changes

15
00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.890
the verb after it, and the other doesn't.
